id: pm-9gzr4r
title: "The edge-count floor is denominated over a population that includes the edges the graph itself calls redundant, so repairing 73 witnessed implied ordering rows and silently relaxing the guard are the same privileged act"
description: "pm graph redundancy computes 73 transitively implied ordering edges (35 blocks + 38 blocked_by), each carrying a witness path, so the product already names them as adding no ordering information. graph-profile-edges-floor is denominated in TOTAL deduplicated directed edges and stands at 11871 against 11875 observed, so the gate-admissible repair is at most 4 of 73 (5.5%). Beyond that the run reports floor_undercut, and --update resolves floors with Math.max, so the gate cannot absorb the reduction either. The declaration's own note anticipates this and prescribes a hand edit of the number. That is the defect: in the resulting diff, repairing a witnessed defect population and silently relaxing a quality floor are byte-indistinguishable acts, both requiring the same privileged edit, so the guard cannot tell a cleanup from an erosion. Denominating the floor over informative edges (total minus redundant) makes the two motions distinguishable without any privileged act: removing an implied edge drops both terms and is neutral, while removing a load-bearing edge still breaches. Dual of pm-c90tfh, which owns the ADDITION direction (the blocks ceiling sits at 243 with zero headroom, so ordering edges cannot be added either); together the two mean the ordering relation is frozen in both directions while three open items require changing it."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: enforcement,graph,measurement-ratchet,redundancy,tracker-governance
created_at: "2026-08-10T20:46:45.822Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-10T20:58:25.675Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: "The floor is re-denominated over a derived measurement (total deduplicated directed edges minus the redundancy analytic's implied ordering rows) declared as pm data, not as a patch to a gate script; redundant_count carries a declared ceiling so the witnessed implied-ordering population can only shrink; Removing a witnessed implied edge is bound-neutral and removing a load-bearing edge still breaches, proven by a negative control in both directions; Lowering any floor requires a linked Decision item, so a repair and an erosion are no longer the same hand edit of a number"
parent: pm-96h7
risk: medium
confidence: 90
actual_result: "graph-profile-edges-floor floor=11871 observed=11875 (headroom 4); pm graph redundancy redundant_count=73; removing 5+ redundant edges fails the release gate with floor_undercut; scripts/release/tracker-measurement-gate.mjs resolves floors with Math.max(declaration.floor, entry.observed) so --update never lowers one"
